From: shaohong.dong <shaohong.dong.cq@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glx: invalidate cached GL context after provider probing

Mesa DRIL queries configurations through a temporary EGL display. On
Adreno, terminating that display changes GL dispatch even while the
original context remains reported as current. Glamor then uses stale
dispatch because lastGLContext still matches its context, resulting in
invalid shader objects and incomplete framebuffers.

Invalidate the context cache after every provider probe, so the next
glamor operation performs its existing unbind/rebind sequence.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: shaohong.dong <shaohong.dong.cq@gmail.com>

--- a/glx/glxext.c
+++ b/glx/glxext.c
@@ -548,6 +548,11 @@
 
         for (p = __glXProviderStack; p != NULL; p = p->next) {
             __GLXscreen *glxScreen = p->screenProbe(pScreen);
+            /* Provider probing can initialize and terminate a temporary EGL
+             * display, changing GL dispatch outside the context cache.
+             * Make glamor rebind its context before its next operation.
+             */
+            lastGLContext = NULL;
             if (glxScreen != NULL) {
                 LogMessage(X_INFO,
                            "GLX: Initialized %s GL provider for screen %d\n",
